Data: 

Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024.csv 
 
Q1 - Budget & Risk Priority 

"We're a healthcare organization that has experienced several cyber incidents. Based on industry data, which attack types are causing the greatest financial damage and affecting the most patients — and where should we be focusing our security budget?" 

Uses: Attack Type × Financial Loss + Number of Affected Users, filtered to Healthcare 

Viz: Dual-axis bar chart or bubble chart 

Interesting angle: The most frequent attack may not be the most costly — that tension is worth showing 

Q2 - Defense Effectiveness 

"We currently use a mix of firewalls, VPNs, and antivirus software. Are these tools actually reducing our exposure, or are we investing in the wrong defenses?" 

Uses: Defense Mechanism × Financial Loss + Incident Resolution Time 

Viz: Heat map or grouped bar chart comparing avg. loss by defense type 

Interesting angle: AI-based detection vs. traditional tools — does newer = better? 

Q3 - Recovery Speed 

"After a breach, how long should we expect to be impacted? And are some attack types leaving us exposed for longer than others?" 

Uses: Attack Type × Incident Resolution Time, filtered to industry 

Viz: Box plot or bar chart showing avg/median resolution time by attack type 

Interesting angle: A fast but expensive attack vs. a slow cheap one requires very different response planning 
